{
  "id": "the-harrowing-of-minerva-damson",
  "title": "The Harrowing of Minerva Damson",
  "subtitle": "Magic, Monsters, and the Trenches of World War One",
  "description": "It is March, 1915 in France, and just behind the front lines a woman is running for her life. She does not run from enemy soldiers or falling mortars; a far more sinister creature stalks her, one created by bloodshed and black magic. This is the newest threat in a war growing uglier by the day, and it won't be the last. Or the worst. But this woman is not a civilian. As a knight of the Order of Joan, she is only one of a legion of women with a long history of monster hunting. So when she runs, she does not do so blindly; it's all part of the larger plan. The Harrowing of Minerva Damson is an action-horror podcast. Interested in supporting the Order and its knights? Join us on Patreon at patreon.com/theharrowingofminervadamson , or donate on Acast at supporter.acast.com/the-harrowing-of-minerva-damson . If you'd like to browse the latest Order war bulletins, you can visit our website at www.orderofjoanheadquarters.com or follow us on Instagram @theharrowingofminerva . The Harrowing of Minerva Damson is a Goblin Booth Production. Listen to the latest episodes, browse merch, and discover more of our programming on our YouTube channel, Goblin Booth Productions , or our website here . Support this show http://supporter.acast.com/the-harrowing-of-minerva-damson . Hosted on Acast. See acast.com/privacy for more information.",
